# Development Plan — Chain-to-Cloud Voting

This document expands **Section 5: High Level Architecture** from `architecture.mdc` into a concrete, phased development plan.

Five phases are **balanced in scope**: each phase delivers a coherent slice of the system and includes infrastructure, application code, observability, and quality work.

---

# Relationship to Architecture

The high-level flow from `architecture.mdc` is:

| Phase   | Architecture summary |
|--------|------------------------|
| **Phase 1** | Blockchain → Ingestion Lambda (TypeScript) → SNS/SQS → Aggregator (Go) → DynamoDB → **gRPC API** (for UI) |
| **Phase 2** | SQS → Forwarder Lambda → GCP Pub/Sub → Analytics (Go) → BigQuery; **UI first slice** (Elixir/Phoenix LiveView) |
| **Phase 3** | **Global voter eligibility:** Merkle allowlist on-chain + admin grant/revoke; one vote per wallet per proposal |
| **Phase 4** | Event backbone: Kafka (opt.); **UI full slice** (streaming, trends); Grafana, E2E, runbooks |
| **Phase 5** | **Voting playground:** primitive voting UI (on-chain) + **simulation orchestrator** (many simulated voters / event injection) to observe full pipeline |

This plan breaks each phase into **deliverables**, **infrastructure**, **services**, **observability**, and **quality** so that effort is distributed evenly.

---

# Phase 1 — MVP: Operational Pipeline (AWS)

**Goal:** End-to-end flow from blockchain to operational read model and a minimal read API. All on AWS.

## 1.1 Scope Summary

- Smart contract emits structured events.
- Ingestion captures events and publishes to SQS.
- Aggregator consumes SQS, maintains DynamoDB projections, exposes **gRPC read API** (designed for the user interface; see Phase 2).
- Basic observability and CI/CD in place.

## 1.2 Deliverables

### Smart contract

- **Stack:** Rust, Solana Anchor (or alternative per architecture).
- **Surface:** `create_proposal(title, options[], voting_ends_at)` (or duration at create), `vote(proposal_id, option_id)`, `close_proposal(proposal_id)`.
- **Single active proposal:** At most one proposal in open voting at a time; `create_proposal` rejects while another is open. See **architecture.mdc** §8.
- **Voting window:** Enforced **on-chain** — reject invalid `vote` when closed or past deadline; emit `voting_ends_at` on `ProposalCreated` when used. See **architecture.mdc** §8 and **event_schema.mdc**.
- **Events:** `ProposalCreated`, `VoteCast`, `ProposalClosed` — data-rich, consistent with `event_schema.mdc`.
- **Tests:** Unit / integration tests per `testing_smart_contract.mdc` (including vote after close / after deadline rejected).

### Ingestion service

- **Runtime:** AWS Lambda (Node.js 20).
- **Language:** TypeScript.
- **Responsibilities:** Connect to blockchain RPC/WebSocket, detect contract events, normalize to canonical JSON (including `event_id`, `event_type`, `timestamp`, `source`, `version`), publish to SNS (event bus fan-out).
- **No business logic:** Only capture and normalize; no projections, no DB.
- **Config:** SNS topic ARN, RPC endpoint, program ID from environment.

### Event bus (AWS)

- **Fan-out:** Ingestion publishes to one **SNS topic**; two **SQS queues** subscribe (one for Aggregator, one for Forwarder) so both consumers receive every event. Alternatively, ingestion may publish to two SQS queues. Do not use a single SQS queue for both consumers.
- **SQS:** Each queue has DLQ, visibility timeout and redrive policy aligned with consumer processing time.
- **Terraform:** SNS topic, two SQS queues (and subscriptions), IAM policies, outputs for queue URLs.

### Aggregator service

- **Language:** Go; structure per `service_style.mdc` (cmd, internal/domain, service, repository, handlers).
- **Responsibilities:** Consume messages from SQS, deserialize and validate events, apply idempotent projection updates (dedup/upsert), update DynamoDB.
- **Projections:** Proposals table (proposal_id, total_votes, option_counts, status, updated_at, optional `voting_ends_at` from `ProposalCreated`), VoterActivity table (voter_pubkey, votes_cast, last_vote_timestamp). **Does not define voting duration** — mirrors contract via events; `ProposalCreated` / `ProposalClosed` handlers planned after `VoteCast` (iteration 1).
- **Read API:** **gRPC** API (e.g. ListProposals, GetProposal; streaming in Phase 4) backed by DynamoDB; exposed via API Gateway (gRPC) or gRPC-Web proxy. Contract consumed by the user interface (Phase 2+); see `user_interface/` and `.cursor/rules/user_interface/elixir_ui.mdc`.
- **Eligibility (deferred to Phase 3):** Phase 1 contract may allow any wallet for pipeline demos; **production-usable governance** requires the global Merkle allowlist and admin grant/revoke in Phase 3 (see below).
- **Idempotency:** Required; use event_id or equivalent per `service_boundaries.mdc` and `coding_style.mdc`.
- **Iteration 1 implementation:** `processed_events` table; read-check then apply projections; mark processed only after successful writes; compensating `UndoVoteCast` / `UndoRecordVoteCast` on partial failure or failed mark (see `services/aggregator/`). Unit tests cover duplicate delivery and SQS retry after voter failure.

### Infrastructure (AWS)

- **Terraform:** VPC/network as needed, Lambda (ingestion), SQS, DynamoDB tables, IAM roles (least privilege), API Gateway (gRPC backend or gRPC-Web proxy), CloudWatch log groups.
- **Environments:** At least `dev` and `prod` (or staging) via variables; naming per `terraform_style.mdc`.

### Observability (Phase 1)

- **Logging:** Structured logs (e.g. slog) with correlation fields (event_id, proposal_id, service).
- **Metrics:** Basic CloudWatch metrics (e.g. events published, events processed, errors).
- **DLQ:** Monitor and alert on messages in DLQ.

### Quality and CI/CD

- **Lint and test:** TypeScript test/typecheck for Ingestion; Go lint/test for Aggregator; Rust lint/test for contract; run in CI.
- **Build and deploy:** Build Ingestion Lambda zip (Node.js bundle) and Aggregator Lambda/binary; Terraform plan/apply for AWS (manual or automated apply for prod).
- **Docs:** Repository structure, ADR for major choices, `docs/progress/` entry for Phase 1.

## 1.3 Phase 1 Exit Criteria

- A vote on chain results in an event in SQS, aggregator updates DynamoDB, and the gRPC read API returns updated proposal state (verifiable by a gRPC client or UI in Phase 2).
- Idempotent handling of duplicate events verified, including at-least-once SQS delivery and retry after a failed projection write (Aggregator unit tests; compensating undo, not TransactWrite).
- CI runs lint, tests, and Terraform plan successfully.

### Phase 1 follow-ups (before production-hardened Aggregator)

Tracked here so they are not lost; **not blockers** for closing the first Phase 1 slice (VoteCast + dedup + tests passing).

- **DynamoDB `TransactWriteItems`:** Atomically update `proposals`, `voter_activity`, and `processed_events` in one request instead of mark-last plus compensating undo (stronger consistency on partial failure and mark failure).
- **Concurrent Lambda invocations:** Two workers processing the same `event_id` in parallel can still race despite conditional mark; address with TransactWrite and/or stricter conditional updates when load or ops requirements justify it.

